  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "There's a three-step strategy the ultra-wealthy use to pay almost no tax. It's called buy, borrow, die.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "lock"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Buy. Borrow.",
            "Die."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Step one, buy assets that grow. Step two, borrow cheaply against them instead of selling. Step three, pass them on at death.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "The three steps",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "Buy",
              "value": "assets",
              "note": "stock, property",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 0.6
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "Borrow",
              "value": "tax-free",
              "note": "loans aren't income",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.8
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "Die",
              "value": "reset",
              "note": "heirs pay no gains",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Because you only owe capital gains tax if you actually sell.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-cgt",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · capital gains tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Loans are not income, so borrowing against your stock hands you tax-free cash to live on.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "tax-free",
          "label": "loans aren't income",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "lock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It is textbook tax avoidance, entirely legal use of the rules.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-avoid",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · tax avoidance"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And at death, a rule resets the asset's value, so the heirs owe tax on none of the gains.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "The gains vanish",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That stepped-up basis can wipe out a lifetime of untaxed gains.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-stepup",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · stepped-up basis"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It is the single biggest reason the very richest Americans can pay the lowest real tax rates of all.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Lowest real rates",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So the gains are never taxed, at all. Should that be allowed?",
